<title>HONG KONG: Trading in Hopewell's CEPA ends Dec 11.</title>
<headline>Trading in Hopewell's CEPA ends Dec 11.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The last day for trading in the shares of Consolidated Electric Power Asia (CEPA) will be December 11, the company said following shareholders' approval of the sale of the company to Southern Co.</p>
<p>The announcement was issued late on Monday following the extraordinary general meeting where CEPA shareholders' overwhelmingly approved the Southern proposal.</p>
<p>The company said that under the terms of the sale -- referred to as the &quot;scheme of arrangement&quot; -- the scheme will become effective on or around December 28 and the withdrawal of CEPA's Hong Kong listing effective on or around December 30.</p>
<p>Based on this expected timetable and following the delisting, cash entitlements under the first option and cash and other entitlements under the second option are expected to be posted on or before December 31, the announcement said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6933</p>
